   "daf": "47b",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "עֵד אֶחָד אוֹמֵר רָאִיתִי אֶת הַהוֹרֵג כּוּ׳. טַעְמָא דְּמַכְחֵישׁ לֵיהּ, הָא לָא מַכְחֵישׁ לֵיהּ — עֵד אֶחָד מְהֵימַן.",
   "en": "The mishna taught that if «one witness says: I saw the killer,» and another testifies: You did not see him, they would break the heifer’s neck. The Gemara infers: «The reason» they break the neck «is» because the second witness «contradicts him, but» if «no» one «contradicts him, one witness is relied upon,» and they do not break the heifer’s neck."
  }
